                    "content": "def build_params_model(params_schema: list) -> BaseModel:     \"\"\"     Build a strict Pydantic model from a params_schema.     Unknown fields will raise a validation error.     Note: Vault secrets are always optional in the Pydantic model to allow     for deferred configuration. Required validation happens after vault resolution.     \"\"\"     fields: Dict[str, Any] = {}     for param in params_schema:         name = param[\"name\"]         param_type = param.get(\"type\", \"string\")         field_type = bool if param_type == \"bool\" else str         required = param.get(\"required\", False)         # Vault secrets are always optional in Pydantic validation         # Required validation happens after vault resolution  …
